        <name>DefaultValue</name>
        <qualifiedname>SGRawValue::DefaultValue</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>The default underlying value for this type. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Every raw value has a default; the default is false for a boolean, 0 for the various numeric values, and &quot;&quot; for a string. If additional types of raw values are added in the future, they may need different kinds of default values (such as epoch for a date type). The default value is used when creating new values. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
